  "title": "Answer: no shared position, though Russell located percepts in physical space",
  "statements": [
    {
      "id": "a44b5d54-aec8-4eaa-9d16-b9a51201543f",
      "text": "The family takes no shared position on space. Russell held that physical space is defined causally, so percepts, as causes and effects of physical events, are in physical space inside the percipient’s head. Eddington held space to be derived.",
